# ============================================
# CLOUDINARY ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
# ============================================
# 
# This file shows the required Cloudinary environment variables.
# DO NOT commit actual credentials to version control!
#
# ============================================
# FRONTEND VARIABLES (Vite - used in browser)
# ============================================
# Add to .env file for local development:
#
# VITE_CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME=your_cloud_name
# VITE_CLOUDINARY_UPLOAD_PRESET=your_unsigned_upload_preset
#
# ============================================
# HOW TO SET UP CLOUDINARY UNSIGNED UPLOAD
# ============================================
# 
# 1. Go to https://cloudinary.com/ and sign in
# 2. Go to Settings → Upload
# 3. Scroll to "Upload presets"
# 4. Click "Add upload preset"
# 5. Set:
#    - Preset name: e.g., "portfolio_unsigned"
#    - Signing Mode: UNSIGNED (important!)
#    - Folder: leave empty (we'll set it dynamically)
# 6. Save the preset
# 7. Use the preset name as VITE_CLOUDINARY_UPLOAD_PRESET
#
# ============================================
# CLOUDINARY FOLDER STRUCTURE
# ============================================
# The system uses these folders:
# - portfolio/projects     (for project images)
# - portfolio/certificates (for certificate images)
# - portfolio/tech-stack   (for technology logos)
#
# ============================================
# SECURITY NOTES
# ============================================
# - Unsigned upload is safe for frontend use
# - No API secret is exposed
# - Upload preset restricts allowed operations
# - Consider setting upload limits in Cloudinary settings
#
